1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Ve-AP: an AI agent for the car that has to earn every action.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Agents are coming to cars. A tool list says what they can call, not what they may.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
And a safety rule that has never refused anything has never been shown to work.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:26,000
One predicate guards every vehicle call: eight conditions, each able to refuse on its own.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Each refusal names itself, and all eight are made to refuse on every test run.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Models live above layer 4, protocols below it. Only bounded operations cross.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Two boards in the car, a Jetson and a Raspberry Pi 5, and no cloud.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
MHS, the hardware layer: every hardware fact is checked data, not code.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
The agent never names a pin, a CAN ID or a diagnostic service.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
MHS decides no authority: it can verify an admission, never mint one.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,000
And the device interlock can still refuse a write the gate allowed.

12
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Safety alerts never wait for a model. The agent may explain them, never clear them.

13
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Dangerous capabilities are named only so they can be refused by name.

14
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:43,000
The face leaves as numbers. The road picture leaves blurred, or not at all.

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Nine ideas, each with its evidence: a test count, an eval, or the car.

16
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The model is the last resort: the median answer went from 19.7 s to 0.86 s.

17
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,000
On 19 October every check passed, all eight conditions refused on cue, and the journal was intact.

18
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:26,000
We are starting the Ve-AP framework in the car.
[Terminal blurred: it lists every service as active]

19
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
[Terminal blurred: it lists every service as active]

20
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:35,000
A separate battery powers the Jetson Orin Nano

21
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:41,000
and the Raspberry Pi, the two compute modules,

22
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:51,000
running the vehicle controls, the car views and the camera views.

23
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:59,000
The road camera is a dash cam, and this is the driver-monitoring camera.
[Street blurred for privacy]

24
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:07,000
It is connected over Bluetooth to the car's own audio system.

25
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:15,000
The car's head unit is paired with the Pi.
[Device names blurred]

26
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Here the driver-monitoring model is loading. Once it has loaded, monitoring starts.

27
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,000
This is the GNSS receiver, a Quectel L89.

28
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
It gives position and speed. [No fix on the day; cause not established]

29
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Now the attention view has loaded.

30
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:11,000
It monitors drowsiness. I am acting sleepy on purpose.

31
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:20,000
It detects it: "Signs of drowsiness. Take a break soon."

32
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:30,000
[The face is drawn as lines from numbers. No image of the driver is shown or stored]

33
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:42,000
This is the road view. The dash cam connects to the Pi over Wi-Fi.

34
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:49,000
It shows the objects ahead and the road guidance.

35
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:58,000
The lane model is openpilot, from comma.ai, integrated here.

36
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:02,000
While driving we can see the detail.

37
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:17,000
[Ve-AP blurs the picture before it reaches the screen. Detected objects are boxed]

38
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:32,000
[On this drive the camera sat crooked. Ve-AP refused to calibrate and said: straighten the camera]

39
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Lane lines show when the road has markings. This road has none.

40
00:05:47,000 --> 00:06:00,000
It is a normal local road. On a marked main road the lanes will show.

41
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:19,600
Driver: What is the battery percentage available in this vehicle?

42
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:20,500
[Thinking]

43
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:30,000
Ve-AP: The battery temperature is 25 degrees Celsius; the speed is 54 kilometres per hour;

44
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:37,000
the gear is drive; the battery level is 60 percent; the coolant is 87 degrees Celsius.

45
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Driver: What are the faults in this vehicle?

46
00:06:46,000 --> 00:07:00,000
[Fault codes are read through the gate. In this build the vehicle signals come from a CAN simulator]

47
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,000
Ve-AP: No fault codes are stored in the engine.

48
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Driver: Do you see what trip is ongoing now?

49
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:29,000
[No route is set. The agent will not invent one]

50
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Ve-AP: I don't know the route to there. The simulated routes go to Bengaluru, Madurai, Mysuru, Puducherry.

51
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:44,000
These are the light controls, the battery and energy, and vehicle health.

52
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:50,000
This is software status [read-only: installing is refused by design].

53
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:54,000
And this is driver attention.

54
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:03,000
We enable the cabin camera and open the live view.

55
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:27,000
It is loading the camera model. It is a separate model, so the first load takes time.

56
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,000
We are starting the cabin camera.

57
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:40,000
[It learns this driver's normal first]

58
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Ve-AP: "Stay alert."

59
00:08:44,000 --> 00:09:15,000
[Eyes closed on purpose: closure is judged against this driver's normal]

60
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Ve-AP: "Stay alert."
[On screen: "Signs of drowsiness. Take a break soon."]

61
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:34,000
[The camera was straightened between drives. The mount was found by driving, in 74 s]

62
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:46,000
[The picture is blurred by Ve-AP before it reaches the screen]

63
00:09:46,000 --> 00:10:00,000
[Cars, people and trucks are tracked. The lane model draws the path ahead]

64
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:14,000
["Lens uncalibrated" is shown, not hidden: the lens was never measured]

65
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:24,000
[About 10 frames per second, all through the drive]

66
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:38,000
[Later in the same drive]

67
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:52,000
[Objects in the car's path are flagged "in path"]

68
00:10:52,000 --> 00:11:06,000
[A close hazard in path can be spoken: "Watch out ahead." Its distance thresholds are not yet checked]

69
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Real: cameras, microphone, speech, car audio. Simulated: the vehicle signals. The car's own bus is next.

70
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:26,000
The road view held about 10 fps. It refused a crooked camera, then found the mount in 74 s.

71
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Limits are stated, not hidden. Next: the car's own OBD-II bus, listen-only first.

72
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Docs, diagrams, slides and this film: the ve-ap-capstone repository. Thank you.
